{"id": "86200", "name": "פירוק טרינום ריבועי – מקדם מוביל כללי וסימנים מעורבים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "none", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Factorise the following:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Compare the expression with the expanded general product and find the integer factors that match its coefficients.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The general product</b><br>As can be seen by multiplying out a general, factorised quadratic:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ (cx+a)(dx+b) = cdx^2+(da+cb)x+ab, \\]</p>\\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are factors of the constant term, and \\(c\\) and \\(d\\) are factors of the \\(x^2\\) coefficient so there are only a finite number of (integer) cases that are possible. With practice it should be simple enough to find \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\) and \\(d\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Matching coefficients</b><br>In this example:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}. \\]</p>Equating with the general quadratic above gives:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {cd = {{CT:1}}}. \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {da+cb = {{CT:2}}}. \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {ab = {{CT:3}}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The factorised form</b><br>The correct values are: \\(a = {{CT:4}}\\), and \\(b = {{CT:5}}\\), \\(c = {{CT:6}}\\) and, \\(d = {{CT:7}}\\). By substituting these back into the general quadratic, and factorising constants out, we obtain the factored form:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:8}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "FacForm", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "cf1", "cf2", "ta", "v"], "nvariants": 50}